  era: "c. 2800 BCE \xB7 Section 2 \xB7 Indus Valley Civilisation \xB7 c. 3300 \u2013 1300 BCE (mature phase c. 2600 \u2013 1900 BCE)"
  title: Kalibangan
  text: On the Ghaggar river in Rajasthan, Kalibangan has the earliest ploughed field known, from the Early Harappan phase, as well as fire altars and a citadel. Its name means black bangles.
